# Development method

Before a major feature: state the business problem, contribution to the 800-registration target, minimum implementation, required data, and risks. Implement the smallest working version. Test against representative data. Measure usefulness. Only then expand.

Do not silently expand scope. Explain significant architectural complexity before implementing it.

A feature is done when it works against representative data, errors are handled, relevant tests pass, security is considered, configuration is documented, output is commercially useful, and automated decisions are auditable.

Inspect existing code before creating duplicates. Reuse services. Keep changes small enough to test. Run relevant tests after changes. Do not report a feature complete until tested.

Keep the system maintainable by a very small team. Reliability over impressive complexity. Never add dependencies without a clear reason.
